    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Kenia’s capstone project was inspired by her time volunteering as a tutor at Sequoia High School and realizing the need to connect students, all of whom were Spanish-speaking, recent immigrants, with resources related to post-secondary education opportunities. She worked with educators at Sequoia High School, as well as students, to develop a booklet of resources she presented to 45 students during a tour of the Stanford campus. The tour was also composed of an educational workshop focused on topics such as obtaining healthcare services, social security, and postsecondary opportunities, and included guest speakers who spoke about their time navigating college as undocumented students.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Zepeda, K. (2024). Beyond Borders: Empowering Undocumented Learners at Sequoia High School. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/wm895kp7556. https://doi.org/10.25740/wm895kp7556.",
